-- title:
--   Monomial normal form for varpi at a smooth point
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, let $j_0\colon W(\mathbb F_{q^2})\to k$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $X_0$ be a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $k$ relative to $j_0$: a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law over $k$ together with series $\mathrm{act}(a)$ ($a\in W(\mathbb F_{q^2})$) and $\varpi$ that are endomorphisms of the law, with $\mathrm{act}$ multiplicative and additive for the group law, $\varpi\circ\varpi=\mathrm{act}(q)$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}(a)=\mathrm{act}(\sigma a)\circ\varpi$ for the Witt-vector Frobenius $\sigma$, such that the submodules $\mathrm{Lie}_0$ and $\mathrm{Lie}_1$ of $\mathrm{Lie}\,X_0$ (the intersections over $a$ of the kernels of $\mathrm{Lie}(\mathrm{act}(a))-j_0(a)$, respectively $-j_0(\sigma a)$) are complementary and both invertible $k$-modules, and such that $\mathrm{act}(q)$ has kernel of degree $q^4$. Assume it is not the case that the matrix $\lambda(\varpi)$ of linear coefficients of $\varpi$ annihilates every element of $\mathrm{Lie}_0$ and also every element of $\mathrm{Lie}_1$. Then there exist $2$-tuples $\alpha,\beta$ of power series in $k[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with zero constant terms which are mutually inverse under substitution ($\alpha$ substituted into each $\beta_i$, and $\beta$ into each $\alpha_i$, give $X_i$), such that the ideal generated by the two components of $\varpi$ with $\alpha$ substituted equals the ideal $(X_1,\,X_0^{q^2})$.
--
--   This is the choice of normal formal coordinates at a point of the Drinfeld moduli problem lying off the double points of the special fibre: the condition on $\lambda(\varpi)$ says that $\varpi$ does not kill both eigenlines of the $W(\mathbb F_{q^2})$-action on $\mathrm{Lie}\,X_0$, and in the resulting coordinates the ideal of the kernel of $\varpi$ becomes monomial. It is used, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_smul_add_smul_mem_span_varpi_of_addCoboundary_mem_of_not_and`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormalODModule.exists_smul_add_smul_mem_span_varpi_of_addCoboundary_mem_of_not_and), in the local analysis of deformations of special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules; the proof cites the characteristic-$q$ rank normal form for homomorphisms of formal group laws and the computation that the kernel algebra of $\varpi$ has $k$-dimension $q^2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalODModule_exists_subst_eq_X_and_span_subst_varpi_eq_of_not_and.lean

